From 871ff4dffe9e17656514f80e4fb297670611d2d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:51:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ci: pull the Supabase test images from GHCR first

test-e2e's anonymous public.ecr.aws pulls fail with toomanyrequests on shared runner IPs, before
any test runs (main run 39465074029, PR 19 run 39510640048).

The pre-pull moves into scripts/ci-prepull-images.sh. The three Supabase images are taken from
ghcr.io/supabase (identical manifest digests) and tagged back to their public.ecr.aws names, so
Compose and production keep their names. public.ecr.aws is the fallback in every attempt.

Unchanged: the image list derived from the Compose file and Dockerfiles, the skip of images that are
already present, six attempts and the growing backoff.

New harness test scripts/ci-prepull-images.test.mjs runs the real script against stub docker and
sleep binaries, and is wired into test:harness.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HxsZ7tmGHEy4wbta427fyF
